{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy this file to carts.local.json and edit it. carts.local.json is",
    "GITIGNORED and must stay that way: it names a directory on your machine",
    "and the filenames of your cartridges, and cartridge firmware is strictly",
    "local. Nothing here is ever committed, bundled, or fetched from anywhere.",
    "",
    "server.ps1 mounts 'dir' READ-ONLY at /carts/ and binds localhost only, so",
    "it is reachable from this machine and nowhere else. The files stay where",
    "they are; nothing is copied into the repository. GET and HEAD only -- any",
    "write method is refused with 405.",
    "",
    "'slots' maps each slot on the Game Boy page (play/gameboy/) to a filename",
    "inside that directory, so clicking a slot loads it with no file dialog. Any",
    "slot you leave out simply falls back to the file picker, and so does every",
    "slot if this file or the directory is absent. The page works perfectly well",
    "with no cartridges at all -- it just asks each time.",
    "",
    "The slot names are the core's ladder rungs and come from the vendored",
    "play/gameboy/web/shell.js. If a core update changes that list, the page's",
    "slots change with it and this file needs no edit -- unmapped slots are",
    "simply pickers."
  ],

  "dir": "C:\\path\\to\\your\\GameBoyFiles",

  "bios": "",

  "slots": {
    "tetris": "",
    "drmario": "",
    "marioland": "",
    "sml2": "",
    "zelda": "",
    "prehistorik": "",
    "pinball": "",
    "disneyland": ""
  }
}
